  "prompt": "Are doctors' professional fees subject to VAT?",
  "runtimeCommit": "d71b913ddf39726234dd02d858fac3e5275e865b",
  "answer": "### Issue Presented\nAre doctors' professional fees subject to Value-Added Tax (VAT)?\n\n### Short Answer\nDoctors' professional fees are generally subject to VAT unless specifically exempted under the National Internal Revenue Code (NIRC).\n\n### Legal Interpretation\n\n### Practical Application\nIn practice, doctors should assess whether their services qualify for any VAT exemptions under the NIRC. If their services are not exempt, they must register as VAT taxpayers and charge VAT on their professional fees. It is advisable for medical practitioners to maintain proper documentation and consult with tax professionals to ensure compliance with VAT regulations and to determine if any specific exemptions apply to their practice.",
